    "declarations": "Two long arms and two bent hind legs are painted. The far foot is a small horizontal patch behind the near forearm, with its proximal chain partly occluded; its hip/knee coordinates are fit hypotheses, not directly visible internal joints. The unchanged automatic silhouette observer counts only three ground clusters because the far foot and near hand share a connected lower silhouette. This packet does not override that measurement or assert four independently separated ground contacts. The right arm ends in partly open curled fingers, not a clean flat knuckle pad. Terminal heights differ by roughly 25–40 pixels; grounded movement and finger/hand skin quality remain unmeasured. No tail is painted and the named Gorilla is an ape. The existing primate absent-tail contract is used; no tail or independently articulated ear is invented. Head, beard and nape boundaries need moving-paint review.",
